<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>Do you save my course grades on your servers?</h3>
    <p>No, we structurally cannot see or permanently capture your confidential numeric grades. This tool operates entirely client-side, executing locally inside your computer's browser. This ensures total privacy protection while also allowing the calculator to work exceptionally fast without delays.</p>
    
    <h3>Does this handle plus and minus grading scales accurately?</h3>
    <p>Yes. The interactive dropdown inherently includes standard fractional multiplier modifications used universally across modern collegiate grading systems (e.g., A- is 3.7, B+ is 3.3). This accurately reflects those subtle numeric changes properly.</p>
    
    <h3>How do pass/fail credits affect my final calculation?</h3>
    <p>Standard registrars completely ignore pass and fail classifications when calculating an official numeric grade point average. A passing grade gives you the academic credit toward graduation, but carries no quality points, so you should formally omit them from the calculator to avoid distorting your true GPA.</p>
</section>

